. The argument's u_t notation is understood as the time derivative of the supplied smooth map; the packet consistently uses r for the positive second-coordinate value. The scalar a is explicitly supplied by H002.\",\n      \"locations\": [\"/parameters/2\", \"/inputs/0/statement\", \"/inputs/1/statement\", \"/output/statement\", \"/inference/argument/0/text\"]\n    },\n    \"object_closure\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The point variables are introduced as arbitrary locals; u, n, m and Δ_x are declared in the parameters and D003. The scalar a is introduced from H002's existential at the fixed point. Derivatives are available from the declared smoothness of u and Δ_x from D003.\",\n      \"locations\": [\"/parameters\", \"/definitions/0\", \"/inference/locals\", \"/inference/argument/0/objects\"]\n    },\n    \"dependency_closure\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Actual factual uses in S001 trace to H001, H002, the smoothness in the parameter declaration, D003, and the explicitly permitted finite-dimensional calculations. No ancestor proof or unlisted theorem is needed.\",\n      \"locations\": [\"/parameters/2\", \"/definitions/0\", \"/logic/calculations/0\", \"/inference/argument/0\"]\n    },\n    \"packet_replay\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"notes\": \"The mathematical sufficiency review used only the complete packet and declared Yui procedure; no source proof, other inference body, prior audit, or external mathematical material was used. The actual input boundary is packet.json plus the relevant declared Yui rules. The available execution record does not establish carrier identity or isolation, so I cannot certify those replay conditions.\",\n      \"locations\": [\"/packet_sha256\", \"/warning\", \"/inference/argument/0\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"findings\": []\n}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_ta